winit: build the Wayland and X11 backends on Haiku

winit's free_unix alias already takes in Haiku; three gaps remain:
- Wayland is chosen without WAYLAND_DISPLAY/WAYLAND_SOCKET on Haiku: libwayland-client's server runs
  in process there (the wayland-client patch connects to it), so there is always one.
- is_main_thread(): as on NetBSD (the Rust main thread's name); Haiku's main thread's id is the
  team id, but the libc crate has no find_thread() binding.
- AsFd/AsRawFd for EventLoop (public, x11 and wayland): left out on Haiku, where calloop has no
  poller fd (polling's poll(2) backend; the calloop patch). Nothing in Photocraft's graph uses them.
Applies with -p1 to winit 0.30.13.

